{"sequence":31,"timestamp":"2026-03-27T17:13:11.962709680Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-7ec97029","body":"In shrimp.rs, four private helper functions (shrimp_feeding, update_condition, update_molt_stress, emit_molt_stress_warning) still accept a `_volume_l: f64` parameter that is now dead code — each function either calls `state.water_volume_l()` or uses TankState concentration helpers internally. Remove the unused parameter from these private functions to avoid confusion and dead-code drift. The caller `step_daily_shrimp` already computes `volume_l` but it is only used as a zero-check guard; the helpers no longer need it passed in.","dedup_key":"6fba2a161253f181f3fca3309ee8200d4624815c8aefcc9bfa7797845d5068f8","run_id":"run-20260327155320","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":32,"timestamp":"2026-03-27T17:13:11.971978806Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-b9d261ac","body":"In nitrogen_cycle.rs line 83, the decomposer DO Monod term uses a hardcoded half-saturation constant (`do_total / (do_total + 2.0)`) with a comment '// half-sat ~2 mg total'. This constant should be extracted into ProcessParams (e.g., `decomposer_k_do_mg`) alongside the existing `decomposer_k_doc_mg`, so it is tunable and consistently documented. Currently it is the only hardcoded Monod K constant in the nitrogen cycle; all other guilds (AOB, NOB, comammox) have their K values in ProcessParams.","dedup_key":"76b0e71fef160b3d6d1c853cfcd3445a81d89663ac34c9e78ebe9ba1f0dea860","run_id":"run-20260327155320","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":33,"timestamp":"2026-03-27T17:13:11.981332039Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-2-7a74aad7","body":"Fix the zero-volume startup override path in `crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs:546-600`. When `source_water_profile_id` is `None`, substrate-only overrides rescale the existing totals instead of rebuilding from the scenario’s source water. That breaks as soon as the original materialized state has `old_volume_l <= f64::EPSILON`: `WaterState::rescale_totals_for_volume` in `crates/tank_core/src/types/water.rs:179-184` returns a zero scale in that case, so switching to a shallower substrate after a low-fill materialization leaves a positive `water_volume_l()` but zero nitrate/alkalinity/calcium/etc. Repro: `medium_planted` with `fill_ratio=0.1`, `source_water_profile_id=None`, `substrate_preset=InertSand` produces ~0.36 L of water with all dissolved totals still at 0. Rebuild from the effective source-water profile (or at least special-case `0 -> positive` volume changes) and add a regression test for this path.","dedup_key":"840c0a2a40b6c0eaa544139c9e8e7fdf4e56d082956385adcfbfa27ef4146136","run_id":"run-20260327155320","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
