{"sequence":80,"timestamp":"2026-03-27T18:50:28.081531836Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-5-d6a4b57a","body":"In nitrogen_cycle.rs, the local `concentration_from_total()` function (line 383-389) exactly duplicates the private `concentration()` function in water.rs (line 301-307). Extract this shared logic to a `pub(crate)` function (e.g., in water.rs or a shared utilities module) so there is a single canonical implementation. Currently, if the safety checks (NaN/Inf handling, EPSILON threshold, non-negativity clamping) are updated in one copy, the other copy silently diverges.","dedup_key":"ca8ab5355a07a5634ca57c116eb5dbc12599a24da77ae6d37fa9ab1c13b90593","run_id":"run-20260327155320","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
{"sequence":81,"timestamp":"2026-03-27T18:50:28.090218602Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-5-4a64f0c3","body":"algae_growth.rs uses `state.water.tan_mg_n_per_l(volume_l)` (the WaterState method taking volume_l directly) while plant_growth.rs, shrimp.rs, events.rs, and snapshot.rs use `state.concentrations()` (the ConcentrationView pattern). Standardize algae_growth.rs to use `state.concentrations()` like the other systems, so the volume is computed once via the canonical `water_volume_l()` path and the calling pattern is consistent across all systems.","dedup_key":"ef3788344532b3fe060221ed424eb8016a977facf774513dc8eea25cb6c52f0f","run_id":"run-20260327155320","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
