{"sequence":94,"timestamp":"2026-03-27T19:14:41.261036364Z","event_type":"amendment_queued","details":{"amendment_id":"fr-6-1af96a54","body":"In `crates/tank_core/src/systems/plant_growth.rs:9-23`, the water-column concentrations are captured once before the plant loop and then reused at `crates/tank_core/src/systems/plant_growth.rs:59-69`, even though each iteration mutates the shared water pools via `remove_plant_nutrients()` at `crates/tank_core/src/systems/plant_growth.rs:93-134`. Later guilds therefore compute nutrient limitation and health from stale TAN/nitrate/phosphate values after earlier guilds have already depleted the water column. Recompute the water-column factors inside the loop (or after each guild’s removals) so guild-to-guild competition uses current chemistry.","dedup_key":"3809ca898e7ab423ef306e9972eea1425080d027df76a5c60318749e35dc8b5a","run_id":"run-20260327155320","source":"workflow_stage","source_stage":"final_review"}}
